{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CexnSZMUYThoEquUnxDD6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the independent critic analysis. My final response has been submitted.\n\nTo summarize the situation honestly: I issued a standalone `read_files` action covering both required inspection groups (implementation files `harness/planner.py`, `harness/contract.py`; test file `tests/unit/test_planner.py`), which satisfies the host's mechanical inspection gate. However, the host's interface returned only acknowledgements rather than the actual file bodies. Consistent with the instruction to never claim to have read a file the host has not returned, I:\n\n- Grounded all **confirmed facts** in artefacts whose contents *were* provided (the pinned contract, registry, schemas, `decisions.md`, golden cases, input-catalog snapshot, and prompt rules).\n- Recorded **zero disproved hypotheses**, because disproving any Stage A planner-internal hypothesis (H1–H7) requires the planner/contract/test source that was not surfaced — and I explicitly warn the Work Controller not to read absence of disproof as confirmation.\n- Documented the specific **evidence gaps** (each unsurfaced module and the unprovided per-question schemas) so the host knows exactly what remains uninspected.\n- Preserved the requirements, acceptance hazards, and falsifiable questions as forward-looking planning inputs, each tied to specific repository evidence with a stated disproof condition.\n\nAll workflow, materiality, and pass/fail decisions remain host/Work Controller owned, as required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6329,"cache_read_input_tokens":88312,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6329},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"c