{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CexnV9UN44U9GAhjdzcSE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rtq1sfua6AjupUMzkMw8Jg","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"tool_name":"final","arguments_json":"{\"response\":\"# Independent Problem Analysis\\n\\nI issued `read_files` for both required inspection groups — implementation (`harness/planner.py`, `harness/contract.py`) and tests (`tests/unit/test_planner.py`). Each call was accepted by the host, but the file bodies were not surfaced back to me (the host returned only a generic acknowledgement, not source text). Per the honesty constraint I will not claim to have read content the host did not return. Consequently the Stage A planner-internal hypotheses (H1–H7) **cannot be converted into confirmed facts or disproved findings**: the planner and test source that would settle them was requested through the host interface but not returned to me. Everything below is grounded strictly in artefacts whose contents the host did supply: the pinned contract/registry/schemas, `decisions.md`, `golden_cases.json`, `input_catalog.snapshot.json`, and `prompts/rules.md`. This is current-state grounding of the problem *framing*; it does not decide materiality, blocking, pass/fail, or reconciliation — those remain Work Controller decisions.\\n\\n## Confirmed implementation facts\\n\\nConfirmed from repository artefacts whose contents were provided (the contract/config/eval surface the planner must operate within), not from `harness/planner.py` source, which was not surfaced.\\n\\n- **The contract owns per-question input policy, not the harness.** `poc_question_registry.v0.3.0.json` `input_policy` and `question_schemas/v0.3.0/_index.json` both enumerate `required`, `material`, `conditional_material`, `defaultable`, `optional` for every QID. VC-POC-05/06/07 declare `conditional_material: {distance_km: market_definition == distance}`; VC-POC-08 makes `distance_km` unconditionally required/material. The data source for “derive required inputs” exists in the pinned contract.\\n- **Request schemas enforce exact construction mechanically.** `VC-POC-01/03/04.request.schema.json` set `additionalProperties: false`, closed `enum`s, `uniqueItems`, and cardinality (`VC-POC-04.acara_sml_ids minItems: 2`; `VC-POC-03/04 maxItems: 20`). OD-07 keeps the VC-POC-09/10 “at least one explicit filter” rule registry/emitter-enforced (schemas express only `minProperties >= 1`). Schema-exactness is a real, testable obligation.\\n- **The absence classes are contract-defined and non-interchangeable.** `POC_CONTRACT_V0.3_SPEC.md` error boundary and `poc_evidence_error.v0.3.0.schema.json`: a directory-absent `acara_sml_id` is `bad_request`; a directory-valid record lacking geography/coordinate is `unanswerable`; a well-typed value matching no fact is a successful `empty`/`partial` result. `error_kind` enum: `bad_request | unknown_question | excluded_question | unanswerable | data_unavailable | internal`.\\n- **`excluded_question` requires a registry reason_code.** The error schema `allOf` requires `reason_code` when `error_kind == excluded_question`; VC-POC-14 carries `not_yet_validated`. Gated/excluded outcomes are legitimate abstentions, structurally separate from a planner defect.\\n- **The metric-list distinction is real and named.** `poc_input_catalog.v0.3.0.schema.json` `x-poc-request-field-to-catalog-list` maps `VC-POC-01.metrics`/`VC-POC-04.metrics` → `profile_metrics` but `VC-POC-11.metrics` → `student_context_metrics`; `input_catalog.snapshot.json` confirms `student_context_metrics` is a strict subset of `profile_metrics`. Wrong-list selection is a concrete, gradeable hazard (G-5).\\n- **The single-source input catalog exists and is non-provisional.** `prompts/input_catalog.snapshot.json` has `\\\"provisional\\\": false`, `contract_version 0.3.0`; ADR-015 states it is read by both the prompt generator and the fixture builder.\\n- **The interim conditional-materiality defect is documented as open.** `decisions.md` O-8: the materials gate treats `distance_km` as unconditional and accepts a needless clarification on SA2 markets, pinned by a strict `xfail` in `tests/unit/test_agent_loop.py`. O-1: v0.3.0 adoption should delete three interim shims including `settings.MATERIAL_INPUTS`. Documented current state, not resolved.\\n- **The failure-taxonomy doctrine the request invokes is established.** ADR-016 (an implementation failure is never folded into a quality metric) and ADR-014 (`RepairCapExceeded` carrying the data layer message to an `Unsupported`) are the design context for requirement 5.\\n- **Golden cases already encode the target behaviours.** `golden_cases.json` (contract_version 0.3.0) carries `expected_request`, `unordered_request_keys`, `expected_missing_inputs` (`clarify/distance_km-conditional` → VC-POC-05 missing `distance_km`; `clarify/market_definition`), refusal cases with pinned reason text, the gated `refuse/gated-forecast` VC-POC-14 case, and three injection cases.\\n\\n## Disproved initial hypotheses\\n\\n- **None can be honestly disproved at this stage.** Disproving any of H1–H7 requires the source of `harness/planner.py`, `harness/contract.py`, `harness/intent.py`, `config/settings.py`, and the planner/agent tests. My `read_files` actions for these paths were accepted by the host, but no file bodies were returned to me, so I record **zero disproved hypotheses** rather than fabricate a determination. The Work Controller must not read the absence of disproof as confirmation.\\n\\n## Unresolved evidence gaps\\n\\n- **`harness/planner.py` body not surfaced** — the central artefact. Cannot verify contract-sourced vs `settings.MATERIAL_INPUTS`-sourced derivation (H1), code-owned vs model-delegated determinism (H2), or request-construction logic.\\n- **`harness/contract.py` not surfaced** — cannot confirm whether `material_inputs_for()` can express conditional materiality or still cannot (the O-8 claim), nor whether it reads `_index.json`/registry.\\n- **`harness/intent.py` (and `outputs.py`, `errors.py`, `tools.py`) not surfaced** — cannot confirm union-branch selection (answer/clarify/refuse/Unsupported), how `classify()`/`_by_status` and `RepairCapExceeded` map `error_kind`s to outcomes, or where the planner sits on the model/code seam.\\n- **`config/settings.py` not surfaced** — cannot confirm whether the `MATERIAL_INPUTS` shim still exists post-v0.3.0 adoption (O-1).\\n- **`tests/unit/test_planner.py`, `test_agent_loop.py` bodies not surfaced** — cannot confirm the O-8 `xfail` is present as described, what `test_planner.py` asserts, or whether determinism is exercised via `evals/replay.py`.\\n- **Per-question request schemas for VC-POC-05/06/07/09/10/12/13/14 not provided** — only 01/03/04 bodies were supplied. Conditional `distance_km`, filter minimums, defaults, and the gated schema were reasoned from registry/`_index.json`, not from the schemas themselves.\\n- **`root0:work/20260908T113118/request.md` not provided** — framing rests on the `root2:request.md` copy (identical per Stage A).\\n\\n## Requirements and risks that remain valid\\n\\nThese survive regardless of the unseen implementation, being anchored in provided contract/decision artefacts:\\n\\n- **R1 — Contract-sourced, deterministic derivation of required inputs.** Policy lives in the pinned registry/`_index.json` (ADR-001, ADR-008). Residual dependence on `settings.MATERIAL_INPUTS` (O-1) would violate it — unverified.\\n- **R2 — Safe school resolution.** `prompts/rules.md` step 1 and `poc_school_directory.v0.3.0.schema.json` require directory resolution, batching multiple named schools, multi-match clarification, no name-matching; directory-absent ID = `bad_request`, directory-valid-missing-geography = `unanswerable`.\\n- **R3 — Metric normalization and minimality.** Correct `profile_metrics` vs `student_context_metrics`, `teaching_fte` mapping, and “omit metrics when none named” are pinned in `rules.md` step 2 and the catalog map (G-5).\\n- **R4 — Schema-exact construction.** `additionalProperties:false`, enums, `uniqueItems`, cardinality (VC-POC-04 ≥2), and the VC-POC-09/10 explicit-filter rule are contract-enforced; `request` must echo exactly what the harness supplied.\\n- **R5 — Planner-generated bad requests surface as failures, not `Unsupported`.** The crux: ADR-016/ADR-014 forbid folding an implementation defect into a refusal/quality outcome; genuine `unknown_question`/`excluded_question`/`unanswerable`/`empty` handling must be preserved.\\n- **Compatibility guarantees to verify, not assume:** the contract is pinned by hash and must not be edited (ADR-008/`PINNED.json`); registry version must stay 0.3.0; the O-8 conditional-materiality trap and the G-4 prose-parsing dependency for `distance_km` must not be replicated by a second hand-maintained table.\\n\\n## Acceptance hazards\\n\\n- **Absence miscategorisation:** treating an empty/partial result or an `unanswerable` (directory-valid, no geography) as `bad_request`, or vice-versa — the contract’s central classification rule.\\n- **Silent defect absorption:** a planner-malformed request exhausting the repair cap into an `Unsupported`, masking a harness bug (the exact failure requirement 5 targets; ADR-014/ADR-016). An acceptance test should assert a deliberately malformed planner output surfaces as a planner/internal failure, not a user refusal.\\n- **Wrong metric list / over-inclusion:** `student_context_metrics` vs `profile_metrics` (G-5); adding related-but-unrequested metrics; emitting `metrics` when none were named.\\n- **Unconditional `distance_km` (O-8):** requiring a radius on SA2/LGA/postcode markets. Note the pinned strict `xfail` — a test that “fixes” this without updating the O-8 entry will fail the suite by design; acceptance must account for that coupling.\\n- **Cardinality/uniqueness breaches:** <2 IDs for VC-POC-04, duplicate array items, or VC-POC-09/10 filter sets lacking an explicit filter.\\n- **Refusal/gating drift:** misclassifying VC-POC-14 `not_yet_validated` or an excluded topic as a planner failure, or the reverse (a planner defect narrated as a contract refusal).\\n- **Non-determinism:** if required-input derivation is model-driven, identical questions may yield differing requests — contradicting “deterministically derive”; testable via `evals/replay.py`.\\n- **Shim residue:** continued reliance on `settings.MATERIAL_INPUTS` or harness-side empty detection that O-1 says v0.3.0 adoption should delete.\\n\\n## Falsifiable questions for planning\\n\\n1. Does `harness/planner.py` read materiality/defaults from the pinned registry/`_index.json`, or from `settings.MATERIAL_INPUTS`? **Disproof of shim-dependence:** the value flows from a registry loader with no `MATERIAL_INPUTS` reference.\\n2. Can `contract.material_inputs_for()` express `conditional_material` (the `distance_km`/`market_definition` link), or does O-8 still hold? **Disproof of the O-8 hazard:** the function returns `distance_km` as material only when `market_definition == distance`, and the `xfail` in `test_agent_loop.py` is removed/updated.\\n3. Is the conditional requirement derived from schema `conditional_material` structure, or by string-splitting registry prose (G-4)? **Disproof of brittle parsing:** the planner reads the structured `conditional_material` map, not a `.split()` over prose.\\n4. Where is the answer/clarify/refuse/Unsupported branch chosen, and does a planner-generated `bad_request` route to a distinct failure class? **Disproof of silent absorption:** a test feeds a malformed planner request and asserts a planner/internal failure surfaces rather than a rendered `Unsupported`.\\n5. Is request construction deterministic for identical input? **Disproof of non-determinism:** `evals/replay.py` produces byte-identical `expected_request` across runs for the same phrasing.\\n6. Does the planner select the correct metric list per QID and omit `metrics` when none named? **Disproof of wrong-list risk:** golden cases `answer/VC-POC-11` (student_context) vs `answer/VC-POC-01/04` (profile) and the metric-omission cases pass under `test_planner.py`.\\n7. Are the VC-POC-05/06/07/09/10/14 request schemas actually consistent with the registry policy the planner relies on? **Disproof of schema/registry drift:** a direct read of those unprovided schemas confirms conditional `distance_km`, `minProperties>=1`, and the gated shape.\\n\\n(All planner-internal questions above are currently **unresolved**: `read_files` was accepted for both required groups, but the host did not return the file bodies, so no planner or test source could actually be observed.)\"}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":93344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1285},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4fa2370d-4379-4dea-93bf-be11bebc3007","uuid":"3a1df295-d12b-4f93-a567-056c06ccee07","request_id":"req_011CexnV5ksk32XuRjHH2KQd"}
